# Continuation stack depth limit removed (T-908)
#
# As of T-908, the MAX_CONTINUATION_STACK limit has been removed from LLT's CEK evaluator.
# Tinct runs as a single-process CLI with no multi-tenant threat model, so the OS enforces
# memory limits via OOM. The previous limit caused false positives for legitimate deeply-recursive
# programs (like trace.llt processing large profiling streams).
#
# Deeply nested evaluation is now limited only by available memory and OS stack limits
# (ulimit -s unlimited in justfile means Rust stack won't overflow in most cases).
#
# For tail-recursive programs, TCO (Tail Call Optimization) ensures O(1) stack space.
# See tco_*.llt-eval tests for TCO verification.
#
# This file is retained as documentation that the limit was intentionally removed.

# Simple test to verify no depth limit
[f: [fn [let self n] [if [= n 0] 0 [+ 1 [call self self [- n 1]]]]]
 result: [call f f 50]]
=== out
Int(50)
